$DIR/main.p:12:18: cannot use &p (value of type *Plain) as Dropper value in variable declaration: *Plain does not implement Dropper (missing method Drop)
    d is declared as Dropper, so it can only hold values whose type has every
    method of Dropper.
    Dropper needs a method Drop() (declared on line 8), and *Plain has no method
    of that name. A type satisfies an interface by having all its methods;
    nothing else needs to be declared.
    (see "Interface types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.9)
    (run "pluto explain E0021" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:14:13: Plain.Drop undefined (type Plain has no field or method Drop)
    Plain has type Plain, declared on line 6, which has no field or method Drop.
    Its fields and methods are n.
    (see "Selectors" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.7)
    (run "pluto explain E0076" for a longer explanation)
